Also keep in mind that a maxed luckstone completely negates the to-hit
penalty for using weapons at the unskilled level.  For example,
unskilled dwarvish mattocks will miss A LOT in the early/mid game, but
you can become artifically great with them just by carrying a maxed
luckstone.  This means that the luckstone can save you weapon slots,
and it can allow early/mid characters to use weapons they would
otherwise be unable to use.

It even completely negates the to-hit penalty for using unskilled two-
weapon combat with unskilled weapons.  It would normally be a horrible
idea to use two-weapon combat without spending any of the appropriate
skill slots, but the luckstone allows you to essentially bypass a
giant chunk of the skill slot system.



